# AutomaticWatering

3-zone automatic plant watering system running on an **Arduino UNO R4 WiFi**. Each zone monitors soil moisture and temperature, drives a relay-controlled pump when the soil gets too dry, and stops when it is wet enough. A 240×240 TFT display shows live readings and connectivity status. Arduino IoT Cloud provides remote monitoring and manual pump overrides from anywhere.

## Hardware

| Component | Part | Connection |
|---|---|---|
| Microcontroller | Arduino UNO R4 WiFi | — |
| Display | 240×240 ST7789 TFT | SPI (CS=10, DC=9, RST=8, MOSI=12, SCLK=13) |
| Temperature sensors | NTC thermistors (10 kΩ, β=3950) | A3, A4, A5 |
| Moisture sensors | Resistive humidity sensors | A0, A1, A2 |
| Pumps | Relay modules | D2, D3, D4 |

## Build & Deploy

```bash
pio run                                          # compile only
pio run -t upload                                # compile and flash
pio device monitor -b 9600                       # open serial monitor
pio run -t upload && pio device monitor -b 9600  # flash and monitor
```

## Configuration

Two files are excluded from the repo and must be created locally:

**`src/passwords.h`** — WiFi credentials:
```cpp
#ifndef PASSWORDS_H
#define PASSWORDS_H
#define SECRET_SSID "your-ssid"
#define SECRET_PASS "your-password"
#endif
```

**`lib/network/thingProperties.h`** — generated by the Arduino IoT Cloud dashboard. Declares cloud variables `ac_h` (String), `ac_t` (String), and `ac_pump1/2/3` (bool), then registers them inside `initProperties()`.

All pin assignments, sensor calibration values, and pump thresholds live in `include/constants.h`.

## How It Works

1. On boot, `setup()` initialises the pumps, display, RTC, and Arduino IoT Cloud connection.
2. `loop()` polls the cloud, reads all six sensors, and refreshes the display every 5 seconds.
3. Once WiFi is available, time is synced from `pool.ntp.org` via NTP and stored in the onboard hardware RTC. The RTC keeps ticking accurately even if the network drops later. Re-sync happens every 24 hours.
4. Pump automation (currently in development) turns a pump ON when humidity falls below 50% and OFF when it reaches 85%. Manual overrides are always available via the IoT Cloud dashboard.

## Project Structure

```
AutomaticWatering/
├── include/
│   └── constants.h      Pin mappings, thresholds, calibration values
├── src/
│   ├── main.cpp         setup()/loop(), pump logic, cloud polling
│   └── passwords.h      WiFi credentials (gitignored — create locally)
├── lib/                 Project modules (see below)
├── doc/                 Module documentation
│   └── time_manager.md
└── platformio.ini       Board config, build flags, library dependencies
```

## Modules

### `sensors`
Reads the NTC thermistors (temperature) and resistive humidity sensors for all three zones. Uses the Beta equation for temperature and `map()` for humidity. Sensor pins are defined in `include/constants.h`.

### `pumps`
Controls the three relay-driven water pumps on pins D2–D4. Exposes `initPumps()` and `setPump(pin, state)`.

### `screen`
Drives the 240×240 ST7789 TFT display over SPI using `TFT_eSPI`. Handles initialisation and renders live sensor readings alongside WiFi/Bluetooth status indicators. SPI pin assignments and driver config live in `platformio.ini` build flags — there is no `User_Setup.h`.

### `time`
Syncs the current time from `pool.ntp.org` via NTP once WiFi is available, then maintains it using the Arduino UNO R4's onboard hardware RTC. Applies EU DST rules automatically (CEST/CET) so no manual offset changes are needed when the clocks change. See [`doc/time_manager.md`](doc/time_manager.md) for full documentation.

### `network`
A standalone `connectWifi()` helper. Currently unused — WiFi is managed by `ArduinoIoTCloud` via `WiFiConnectionHandler`. Kept for reference.

## Dependencies

Declared in `platformio.ini` and installed automatically by PlatformIO:

| Library | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `bodmer/TFT_eSPI` | ST7789 TFT display driver |
| `arduino-libraries/ArduinoIoTCloud` | Cloud connectivity and remote variables |
| `arduino-libraries/NTPClient` | NTP time sync |
| `arduino-libraries/ArduinoHttpClient` | HTTP support for IoT Cloud |
| `knolleary/PubSubClient` | MQTT support for IoT Cloud |

Built-in UNO R4 libraries (`RTC.h`, `WiFiUdp.h`) require no extra installation.
